# CoPo design standard

Read and follow [DESIGN.md](../../DESIGN.md) before changing CoPo UI.
It is the authoritative project design guide and supersedes conflicting
historical design notes. Later explicit user direction takes precedence.

- Keep warm neutral surfaces, ink text, rounded corners, calm spacing,
  subtle borders, and restrained shadows in both light and dark mode.
- Use existing tokens from `shell/src/ui/styles/theme.ts`; regenerate the
  shared tokens and Dashboard stylesheet when values change.
- Example: buttons use `--radius-input`; the buddy preview uses
  `--radius-panel` and `--surface-companion-preview`.
- Preserve the cat artwork and the personalization preview's size/theme sync.
- Keep rounded headings, Pretendard body text, localization, keyboard focus,
  contrast, and reduced-motion behavior.
- Do not reintroduce teal controls, crimson branding, serif headings, or
  nested cards from older guidance.
- Apply this rule to CoPo work only; it does not set other projects' style.
